def _simplify_once(gates: list[Gate]) -> list[Gate] | None:
    """Run one simplification sweep.

    Scans left to right; whenever a gate can cancel or merge with a
    preceding gate that shares a qubit, the rewrite is performed and the
    scan restarts so the newly adjacent gates become visible. Gates between
    the pair must each act on disjoint qubits or commute with the moving
    gate, so sliding it next to its partner preserves the unitary exactly;
    the nearest preceding gate that shares a qubit without commuting blocks
    the search. Identity rotations are dropped on sight. Returns the
    rewritten list, or ``None`` when no rewrite was possible.
    """
